    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d99">

                <pb facs="0321" n="237" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg237"/>

                <head>No. 95.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hunter to Mr. Beach.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-02-28"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 28,
                        1885</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 24.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your dispatch No. 23 in
                    relation to the imprisonment of Mr. J. R. Santos at Manta, I have to inform you
                    that Congress has requested the President to use his efforts to secure a speedy
                    and fair trial and to protect the life and property of the prisoner. The
                    Department has replied that the recourse of rebutting evidence of his intention
                    of not returning to the United States, &amp;c., is still open to Mr. Santos, and
                    his right thereto will be insisted upon.</p>
                <p>You will demand and make every endeavor to secure for Mr. Santos the right of the
                    treaty, especially in the matter of rebutting evidence to show that he retained
                    by intention and act his acquired United States citizenship.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WM. HUNTER,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Second Assistant
                            Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
